 "injuries": [
  {
   "id": "643175",
   "name": "Keenan Allen",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-19T00:12Z",
   "shortComment": "Allen caught eight of 11 targets for 82 yards in Sunday's 26-20 loss to the Titans.",
   "longComment": "With tight end Tyler Warren (groin) inactive, Allen became the preferred option for Daniel Jones when he needed to move the chains, and the veteran wideout led the Colts in catches, targets and receiving yards while setting personal season highs in all three categories. Mo Alie-Cox was on the other end of Jones' only TD pass, however. Allen will take a 26-227-1 line on 40 targets into a Week 7 clash with the Vikings.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "643172",
   "name": "Josh Downs",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-18T23:50Z",
   "shortComment": "Downs caught four of eight targets for 40 yards in Sunday's 26-20 loss to the Titans. He added seven rushing yards on his only carry.",
   "longComment": "The eight targets were second on the Colts to Keenan Allen, but the volume didn't lead to much production. Downs has failed to reach 50 receiving yards in four of six games this season, posting a 24-289-0 line on 42 targets and failing to establish himself as Indy's No. 1 wide receiver in the absence of Alec Pierce (heel). Downs will face a tough test in Week 7 against the Vikings' stingy defense.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "643171",
   "name": "Daniel Jones",
   "pos": "QB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-18T23:46Z",
   "shortComment": "Jones completed 22 of 42 passes for 269 yards and a touchdown with two interceptions in Sunday's 26-20 loss to the Titans.",
   "longComment": "The Colts committed three turnovers in total and also had a blocked punt returned for a touchdown in an ugly loss to the previously winless Titans. Through six games this season, Jones carries a 4:6 TD:INT and career-worst 5.9 YPA as he struggles to find last year's form, but a depleted group of pass catchers that saw tight end Tyler Warren (groin) sidelined (among others) Sunday may be contributing to Jones' woes. He's unlikely to find a rhythm in Week 7 against the Vikings' stingy defense.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "643170",
   "name": "Jonathan Taylor",
   "pos": "RB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-18T23:40Z",
   "shortComment": "Taylor carried the ball 21 times for 94 yards and a touchdown and caught two of four targets for 57 yards in Sunday's 26-20 loss to the Titans. He also lost a fumble.",
   "longComment": "For the fourth time in six games, Taylor came up just short of 100 rushing yards, but his 151 scrimmage yards were a season high, and he got into the end zone for the seventh time in 2026 on a four-yard run in the fourth quarter. His fumble was one of three Indy turnovers on the day, however, and it was Taylor's second lost fumble of the year. While he's on pace for double-digit TDs once again, Taylor's 4.0 YPC would be the worst mark of his career. He'll try to find another gear in Week 7 against the Vikings.",
   "details": null
  },
