   "id": "642534",
   "name": "Alec Pierce",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Injured Reserve",
   "date": "2026-10-15T00:54Z",
   "shortComment": "Pierce was spotted without a cast on his left ankle/heel Wednesday, James Boyd of The Athletic reports.",
   "longComment": "It's a sign that Pierce is progressing in his recovery from a left heel injury that he aggravated during the Colts' Week 2 overtime loss to the Chiefs. The earliest he is eligible to return from injured reserve is Week 7 against the Vikings, and while Pierce opted for rehab and avoided surgery, Boyd believes that the fifth-year wide receiver is not close to a return. Josh Downs popped up on Wednesday's injury report with a hamstring injury, so Keenan Allen could be the Colts' top wide receiver for Sunday's AFC South showdown against the Titans.",
