  {
   "id": "642323",
   "name": "Pharaoh Brown",
   "pos": "TE",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-13T21:17Z",
   "shortComment": "Brown was signed to the 53-man roster Tuesday.",
   "longComment": "Brown is currently listed on the depth chart behind Tyler Warren, Mo Alie-Cox and Drew Ogletree, so it doesn't appear he will have a prominent role anytime soon. The 32-year-old has played for the Browns, Texans, Patriots, Seahawks and Cardinals since entering the NFL in 2017, totaling 74 catches (102 targets) for 752 yards and three touchdowns in 92 regular-season appearances.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642171",
   "name": "Spencer Shrader",
   "pos": "PK",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-12T15:30Z",
   "shortComment": "Shrader made all five of his field-goal attempts and converted on his lone point-after try during Sunday's 34-22 loss to the Steelers on Sunday.",
   "longComment": "Quarterback Daniel Jones led the Colts on six offensive drives during Sunday's loss, though only one of those drives ended with a touchdown. That meant a busy day for Shrader, who made field goals from 57 and 56 yards in the first half before connecting on three more kicks from 22, 40 and 28 yards in the second. His five made field goals were his most in a game since Week 2 of the 2025 season, and he's attempted at least three field goals in each of the Colts' last four games. His 16 made field goals through five regular-season games leads the NFL, and he also leads all kickers with six made field goals from 50-plus yards. The Colts have a juicy Week 6 matchup against the 0-5 Titans on Oct. 18.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641877",
   "name": "Charvarius Ward",
   "pos": "CB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T16:07Z",
   "shortComment": "Ward (groin) is active for Sunday's game against Pittsburgh.",
   "longComment": "Ward ended the practice week Friday by logging a full session, though his participation wasn't enough to avoid a questionable tag. The veteran has since been cleared to play in Week 5, meaning he will start opposite Sauce Gardner.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641747",
   "name": "Arden Key",
   "pos": "DE",
   "status": "Injured Reserve",
   "date": "2026-10-10T17:51Z",
   "shortComment": "The Colts placed Key (hamstring) on injured reserve Saturday.",
   "longComment": "Key sustained a hamstring injury against the Colts in Week 4, and the injury is severe enough for the veteran defensive lineman to warrant a stint on IR. He'll be required to miss at least four games, so the earliest Key can return is Week 9 against the Cowboys on Sunday, Nov. 8. Laiatu Latu, Jaylahn Tuimoloau and rookie fifth-rounder George Gumbs are all in line for more defensive snaps in Key's absence.",
